{"sub":"Monday 23 November 2026 · GBP/USD · London: sell a failed run above Friday's high, Grade C, half size. Updated through the day as the desk posts.","tracker":"<div class=\"tk-row\">\n      <div class=\"tk s-off\" id=\"tkL\"><span class=\"light\"></span><div class=\"lab\"><span>London · SELL GBP/USD (C)</span><em id=\"tkLs\"></em></div><div class=\"bar\"><i></i></div></div>\n      <div class=\"tk s-off\" id=\"tkN\"><span class=\"light\"></span><div class=\"lab\"><span>New York · TBC</span><em id=\"tkNs\"></em></div><div class=\"bar\"><i></i></div></div>\n    </div>\n  ","feed":"<article class=\"post\" data-l=\"wait\" data-lp=\"0\" data-n=\"off\" data-np=\"0\" data-t=\"06:40 UK\"><div class=\"time\">06:40<small>London brief</small></div><div class=\"body\"><span class=\"tag\" style=\"--k:var(--copper)\">London brief</span><h2>Monday: sell a fake break of Friday&#x27;s high, half size.</h2><p class=\"lede\">The dollar slid overnight towards a support area, and the pound is right under Friday&#x27;s high with a sell gap just above. Mondays often fake one way before the real move, so we look to sell a run above Friday&#x27;s high that fails, at half size.</p><div class=\"plan\"><header><strong>GBP/USD</strong><span class=\"side sell\">SELL · GRADE C</span></header><dl><dt>Wait for</dt><dd>A run into <b>1.31332 - 1.31392</b> (from 07:00)</dd><dt>Entry</dt><dd>A 5-minute candle <b>closes back below</b> 1.31332, dollar turning up</dd><dt>Stop</dt><dd>1.31400 · about 7 pips</dd><dt>Target 1</dt><dd>1.31172 Asia high · about 16 pips</dd><dt>Target 2</dt><dd>1.31100 today&#x27;s open · about 23 pips</dd><dt>Cancel</dt><dd>A 15m close above 1.31400</dd><dt>Risk</dt><dd>0.5% (half size) · R:R 3.4</dd></dl></div><div class=\"news\"><header><b>Red news today</b><span>Calendar not fully checked · UK time</span></header><div class=\"none\">No high-impact news for USD, GBP or EUR today.</div></div><div class=\"notes\"><div class=\"nt\" data-lv=\"b\"><h4>In plain English</h4><p>Friday&#x27;s high is 1.31287. Many traders have buy orders and stops just above it, and there&#x27;s a gap where sellers stepped in last week at 1.31332-1.31392.</p><p>If London pushes into that gap and a 5-minute candle closes back below 1.31332 while the dollar starts rising, we sell for a move back to 1.31172 and 1.31100. If the pound keeps climbing, we do nothing.</p></div><div class=\"nt\" data-lv=\"i\"><h4>The trader&#x27;s view</h4><ul><li>Synthetic DXY 103.629: under TDO 103.765 and its Asia low 103.702, heading for the 1h/4h bull FVG 103.567-103.580 above PDL 103.548.</li><li>EUR +0.05%, GBP +0.02% since 05:00: the pound is the weaker, so it&#x27;s the one to sell.</li><li>Week direction not set: Monday is the manipulation day; the weekly rule waits for a tap of an HTF array and the move away.</li></ul></div><div class=\"nt\" data-lv=\"p\"><h4>ICT breakdown</h4><ul><li><b>Bias:</b> none yet for the week; intraday Judas-up into premium, Grade C.</li><li><b>Model:</b> run of PDH 1.31287 into the 15m/1h bear FVG 1.31332-1.31392, CISD back below 1.31332, DXY 5m close up (from its 1h/4h bull FVG).</li><li><b>DOL:</b> Asia high 1.31172 (30m bull FVG 1.31166-1.31221), then TDO 1.31100.</li></ul></div></div><section class=\"stage\" aria-label=\"Session chart\"><header><div><strong id=\"cPair\"></strong><small>15m · UK time</small></div><div class=\"views\" id=\"views\"></div></header>\n<svg class=\"chart\" id=\"chart\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Candlestick chart of the session with the desk's levels\"></svg><div class=\"pdk\" id=\"pdk\"></div><div class=\"scap\" id=\"cap\"></div></section></div></article>","week":"<section class=\"week\"><h3>Meridian 1 · week of 23 Nov · pips on the feed</h3><div class=\"wk\"><div class=\"\"><small>Mon</small><b class=\"\">live</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Tue</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Wed</small><b class=\"\">—</b></div><div class=\"\"><small>Thu</small><b class=\"\">—</b><